{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"16 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,18.453,3.651,3.268,"Nestle India"],[13.889,14.731,26.488,2.373,2.124,"Volume-led growth, full price"],[13.889,20.845,52.954,1.809,1.634,"Nestle India fell 8% on results day (15 October) after Q2 FY27: sales rose 20%"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"to ₹6,782 cr, led by double-digit volume growth, and profit rose 37% to ₹1,030"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"cr (before exceptional items). EBITDA margin was 23.8%, advertising and"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"marketing spend rose 46% YoY, and every product group grew. H1 revenue"],[13.889,26.621,52.951,1.809,1.634,"grew 23%, FY26 15% with volume up 11%. The shares are flat on results day,"],[13.889,28.065,45.813,1.809,1.634,"18% below the August peak, and 12m is flat while NIFTY is up 2.9%."],[13.889,30.551,52.936,1.809,1.634,"1) Momentum is real: NESCAFÉ has grown double-digit for 20 straight"],[13.889,31.995,52.928,1.809,1.634,"quarters, MAGGI keeps expanding rural reach (216,000 villages) and KITKAT"],[13.889,33.439,52.936,1.809,1.634,"is gaining share; GST 2.0 (Sep-2025) added a tailwind now in the base. 2) But"],[13.889,34.883,52.951,1.809,1.634,"the build is not free: A&M is up 46% YoY and stays elevated, cocoa is volatile,"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"food CPI is rising, and management flags near-term consumption softness"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"(Nielsen) and West Asia freight costs; new capacity lifts depreciation. Our"],[13.889,39.216,52.934,1.809,1.634,"FY27E EPS of ₹21.15 is 5% below consensus (₹22.35), which needs H2 sales"],[13.889,40.684,52.934,1.809,1.634,"up 11% and EPS up 13% Y/Y versus our 9% sales and a flat margin. EPS grows"],[13.889,42.128,23.325,1.809,1.634,"18%, 14% and 14% in FY27E-29E."],[13.889,44.59,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,120 averages two methods. Nestle’s own 3-yr average"],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"P/E of 67.5x on earnings twelve months ahead gives ₹1,791; a ten-year DCF at a"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"12% cost of equity, plus net cash and the associate at book, gives ₹457. The gap"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"is the argument: at ₹1,263 the shares need free cash flow to compound 26% a"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"year for a decade; we project 7%. FMCG peers trade at 33.0x forward; the"],[13.889,51.834,52.936,1.809,1.634,"consensus target of ₹1,505 (36 brokers, 22 buys) is +19% above the price. What"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"would prove us wrong: volume-led growth above 15% into FY28 with margin"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"above 24% and FY27 EPS above ₹22. Downside: inflation, consumption"],[13.889,56.167,33.068,1.809,1.634,"slowdown, deeper de-rating of premium multiples."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,67.265,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,050"],[14.451,66.557,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,100"],[14.451,65.851,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,150"],[14.451,65.143,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,200"],[14.451,64.436,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,250"],[14.451,63.73,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,300"],[14.451,63.022,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,350"],[14.451,62.316,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,400"],[14.451,61.607,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,450"],[14.451,60.901,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,500"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,550"],[18.306,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,67.96,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,67.96,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,67.96,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[17.458,69.131,5.603,1.275,1.111,"NESTLEIND ("],[23.065,69.157,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[23.677,69.131,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[26.761,69.131,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.087,70.291,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[26.011,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[31.384,70.291,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.291,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,71